  "summary": "The Burlingame City Council declined to approve an ALPR camera program, with members citing privacy, civil rights, and racial bias concerns and asking for more policy framework, including input from civil rights groups. Police Chief Mike Matteucci reported neighboring cities had no problems with the cameras, and the matter is expected to return in coming months.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Burlingame councilmembers last week indicated they were still unready to approve the use of automated license plate reading cameras within the city, citing a need to further understand how the technology would be applied and how the city could prevent misuse.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "This isn't a bike share program, this is something different, these are policies that have real privacy concerns particularly involved with policing which are under more scrutiny these days, which could have racial bias implications",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "To say that we've heard no ill stories because the only people we've asked are police chiefs, I'm sorry that's not really a great survey",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "The council also discussed the cameras in 2015 but opted not to allow their use. The matter will be brought up again, likely in coming months.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
